# .dockerignore — what must NOT be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS A SECURITY FILE RATHER THAN A PERFORMANCE ONE.
#
# mail-engine/docker-compose.yml builds the engine image with the REPOSITORY ROOT as its context
# (`context: ../`), and mail-engine/docker/engine/Dockerfile does `COPY mail-engine ./mail-engine`.
# Without this file that copy bakes three things into an image layer:
#
#   mail-engine/keys/*.private   the DKIM PRIVATE KEY. Whoever holds it can sign mail that every
#                                receiving server will believe came from edurankai.in. It is already
#                                mounted read-only at runtime, so copying it in is pure leakage.
#   mail-engine/.env             the shared secrets for the application link.
#   mail-engine/.spool/          REAL ACCEPTED MAIL waiting to be delivered.
#
# All three are gitignored, and .gitignore does not apply to a Docker build context — so the single
# mechanism that was protecting them did not cover the one path that ships them off the machine.
#
# The performance benefit is real too (node_modules and .git are hundreds of megabytes streamed to
# the daemon on every build), but it is the secondary reason.

# --- the mail engine's runtime state and secrets ---------------------------
mail-engine/.env
mail-engine/.spool/
mail-engine/keys/
mail-engine/docker/certs/
mail-engine/docker/dovecot/users

# --- application secrets ---------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- bulk, never needed in an image ---------------------------------------
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
dist/
.astro/
.vercel/
downloads/
ml/
.dev-scripts/
face-2fa-portable/
engineering-spec/

# --- scratch that accumulates in this working directory --------------------
*.log
*.html
*.zip
*.backup
